WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.168
A Lottie animation is JSON,

2
00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:05.490
and its words sit
inside text layers.

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.351
Each translation has to fit its box,

4
00:00:08.351 --> 00:00:10.406
use a font that covers the script,

5
00:00:10.406 --> 00:00:11.787
and stay as text.

6
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.144
General Translation's CLI translates
dotLottie files and refits

7
00:00:16.144 --> 00:00:16.851
the layout.

8
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.201
Add a lottie entry and your
fonts to gt.config.json.

9
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.576
Then npx gt stage submits the files,

10
00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:28.733
and npx gt download
fetches each language.

11
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.935
In a test, the full German
label ran past the button,

12
00:00:32.935 --> 00:00:34.652
and the refitted label fit.

13
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.005
Your team now ships
German with each release.
